    "body": "## Summary\n- tag newly created wallet top-up PaymentIntents with explicit `purpose=TOP_UP`\n- reject non-top-up commercial PaymentIntents before payment-ledger mutation\n- preserve compatibility for legacy top-ups created before this change only when they have `topUpRequestId` and no publication marker\n- add regression coverage for explicit top-ups, legacy top-ups, and publication-purpose rejection\n\n## Why\nThe Stripe webhook routes `JOB_PUBLICATION` intents to publication settlement and everything else to the generic wallet top-up service. The generic service therefore must not accept arbitrary or future commercial PaymentIntents as wallet funding. This narrows the trust boundary without stranding already-created legacy top-ups.\n\n## Validation\nNo Flyway migration is required. Merge only after all latest-head CI/checks are green.",
