            "patch_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/dofast/pull/100.patch",
            "merged_at": "2026-08-29T03:27:55Z"
          },
          "body": "## Summary\n- add a dedicated Stripe ledger-settlement entry point for `JOB_PUBLICATION`\n- keep generic wallet top-up settlement restricted to `TOP_UP` and compatible legacy top-ups\n- bind publication settlement to the expected `jobPublicationId` before any ledger or wallet mutation\n- route publication webhook handling through the scoped settlement path\n- add regression coverage for valid publication settlement, cross-publication mismatch rejection, and publication service routing\n\n## Why\nPR #99 correctly narrowed the generic Stripe top-up trust boundary, but the publication settlement service still delegated into that generic path. A valid `JOB_PUBLICATION` PaymentIntent could therefore be rejected after webhook routing. This keeps the trust boundary strict while giving publication funding an explicit, purpose-bound settlement path.\n\n## Validation\nNo Flyway migration is required. Merge only after all latest-head API, web, runtime, publication-payment, ledger and platform-fee checks are green.",
